          },
          "message": "fix: don't pollute stdout with passive update logs (#128)\n\nBug description: scripts that rely on build-tools will fail occasionally\r\nif build-tools hasn't had a recent update check. For example some of my\r\nshell scripts have calls along the lines of `FOO=\"$(e show exec)\"` and\r\nfail when FOO has \"Checking for build-tools updates\" instead of a path.\r\n\r\nWhen the update script is run passively, its stdout is redirected to\r\nstderr: it's still useful there as a user-visible message, but doesn't\r\ninterfere with expected values in stdout.",
          "tree": {
            "sha": "9531e9da96ca7362ea7968e7140b1824a831c8c0",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/electron-build-tools/git/trees/9531e9da96ca7362ea7968e7140b1824a831c8c0"
          },
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/electron-build-tools/git/commits/1f72aa002c6e40277985f1aa92018b126c11c8f4",
          "comment_count": 0,
          "verification": {
